{"diagnosis": "Loopback (divider 64) sent 0xa5 but got 0x25: TRAP: uart data mismatch got 0x25 want 0xa5 with tohost FAIL 0xdead. 0xa5=10100101 vs 0x25=00100101 is an 8-bit to 7-bit truncation / 1-bit right shift. Root cause is picosoc/simpleuart.v:42 `reg [7:1] recv_buf_data` fed from 8-bit recv_pattern and read via reg_dat_do path (picosoc/simpleuart.v:20, picosoc/picosoc.v:124, picosoc/picosoc.v:204), so 0xa5 b[6:0] becomes 0x25.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -39,6 +39,6 @@
 	reg [3:0] recv_state;
 	reg [31:0] recv_divcnt;
 	reg [7:0] recv_pattern;
-	reg [7:1] recv_buf_data;
+	reg [7:0] recv_buf_data;
 	reg recv_buf_valid;

 	reg [9:0] send_pattern;", "expected": "tohost PASS (FAIL 0xdead cleared), TRAP gone, uart loopback 0xa5 matches"}

